# types.ts: FarSunState and SunState.far carry what the body needs to draw itself in the sky pass
#   (true centre while the Sun's set is the frame, share, body turn, spin, times, exposure, burn).
# film.ts: leaveWeight for the Sun is by distance (the globe is drawn while globeShare is above 0), not by u.
#   sunBurn is the body's exposure climb as a function of the camera's place (Sun side by distance from the
#   Sun, Mercury side by Mercury's size in the frame). sun.far is filled in every travel and at every stop after the Sun.
# sky.ts: uSunFar takes the far Sun's share out of the sky's own disc term; the body is drawn at the end of
#   the sky pass with the sky's camera, at the true centre in the Sun's frame, else at sun.dir by angular radius.
